      <p><strong>AMPscript</strong> is the proprietary <em>server-side</em> scripting language of <strong>Salesforce Marketing Cloud Engagement</strong>, designed primarily to personalize content and manipulate data during message and page rendering. With AMPscript, we can generate 1:1 personalized experiences for each contact during message or page rendering.</p>

      <div class="callout">
        <div class="callout-label">📌 KEY CONCEPT · WHY DOES AMPSCRIPT EXIST?</div>
        Unlike client-side languages like JavaScript in a web browser, AMPscript is a server-side language. AMPscript executes on Salesforce servers. In messages, it is evaluated during rendering or the send process; in CloudPages or Landing Pages, it executes when the page is requested and rendered. The end recipient <strong>never sees the AMPscript source code</strong>; they only receive the final rendered HTML or plain text personalized with their data.<br><br>
        <em>Analogy:</em> AMPscript works like a restaurant kitchen. The customer doesn't receive the raw recipe or watch the prep work; they only receive the finished, plated dish at their table.
      </div>

